WEBVTT


00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.358
My name is Cole.


00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.199
And I was head of security
for N-gen Industries.


00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.518
But it was a scientific company
that no one knew about.


00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.078
And for them I murdered


00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.031
and I tortured


00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.230
and I destroyed lives.


00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.591
And I helped them.


00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.476
I helped them create this new world


00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.870
where everything has changed.


00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.555
Everything has changed.


00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.359
Ladies and gentlemen,


00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.995
we live in a society
that becomes more demanding,


00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.112
fast-paced and hectic by the day.


00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.435
To cope with this,
we all need a little help,


00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.677
and as managing director
of N-gen Industries,


00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.349
I'm proud to announce
the arrival of RAK 295,


00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.393
the next generation
of performance-boosting supplement.


00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.990
(Reporter) Mr White,
if RAK 295 has an effect


00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.669
on mental and physical abilities,
how can you be sure it'll be safe?


00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.997
(Mr White) We pride ourselves
on our thorough procedures at N-gen.


00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.714
A full RAK-295 testing programme
is underway


00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.832
with 30,000 volunteers participating.


00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.915
Following two months of assessment,
they will be recalled,


00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.510
fully tested, and the product
will then be available to all.


00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.949
(Reporter) Are you sure
two months is enough time?


00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.231
(Mr White) The work of lead scientist,
Michael Brooke, and my team


00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.112
prior to the testing phase


00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.198
will be there for all to see,
but I can assure you,


00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:49.189
I have no concerns whatsoever
regarding any harmful side effects.


00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.756
- Mr White, I have another question.
- No more questions.


00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.950
(Newsreader) 'The British
pharmaceutical giant, N-gen Industries,


00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.275
'is facing an unprecedented
number of lawsuits.


00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:13.597
'Many of the volunteers who took part
in the drugs trial two months ago


00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.269
'have experienced extreme side effects,
with some becoming seriously ill.


00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.234
'RAK 295 was intended
as a strength and stamina supplement


00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.590
'to cope with the strains
of modern-day life.


00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.234
'Test patients have allegedly suffered
high fevers,


00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.759
'vomiting, internal bleeding,


00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.599
'and in some cases,
multiple organ failure.


00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.280
'Subjects feeling
any side effects whatsoever


00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.072
'are urged to report immediately


00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.476
'to either N-gen laboratories
or to their nearest hospital.'


00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.956
(Screaming)


00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.909
(Choking)


00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.237
Another 12 people were admitted
to St Mary's in Birmingham.


00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.432
And a further 37
to the two hospitals in Manchester.


00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.471
Two more upstairs.


00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.629
So that's all of them,


00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.869
all with failing organs
and vascular collapse.


00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.798
29,999.


00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.997
And her, Angela Mills. Nothing yet?


00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.395
No sign of her?


00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.229
She's not in any hospital in the country.
I want to look at her flat now with Billing.


00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.156
She has a stepbrother in the river service.
Cooper's looking into that.


00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.352
- But what about her parents?
- Died three years ago.


00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.040
White thinks she might be dead.


00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.038
What if she's alive and unaffected?


00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.832
Either way we need to find her.


00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.355
Our glorious CEO
will be paying us a visit later.


00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.391
N-gen, it's finished.


00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.438
Even White's pockets
can't handle 30,000 lawsuits.


00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:02.155
We owe it to these people
to fix what we've done.


00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.192
We'll never be able
to fix what we've done, Michael.


00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.436
It's already too late for that.


00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.475
Listen, look,
I'll be back before White arrives.


00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.079
Just hold it together, yeah?


00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:17.311
(Screaming)


00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.351
- The incident report was inconclusive.
- It's meant to be proof.


00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.392
Your shoulder injury from the struggle
is still our best hope.


00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.592
- So what now?
- We have a much harder battle ahead.


00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.393
The press are...


00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.512
See for yourself.
They've picked a side.


00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.551
I didn't do anything wrong, Morgan.


00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:48.119
I didn't.


00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.912
I'll see you in court next Tuesday.


00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.636
All out of limos.


00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.831
Great to see you.


00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.990
I'll give it all back to you, Steve.


00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.678
Every penny.


00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.870
I'm not bothered about that, mate.


00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.797
Let's just get you back on track, eh?


00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.830
Fuck it!


00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.359
Get over there.


00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.553
- Who the hell are you?
- Never mind me. Who the fuck are you?


00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.511
I'm calling the police.


00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.509
(Groans)


00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.951
(Cole) Check that phone.
Check his numbers.


00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.071
- No!
- Now you listen to me.


00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.873
I'm going to ask you once and once only.


00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.991
Where is Angela Mills?


00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.872
I don't know. I don't know. She...


00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.592
She left two months ago.


00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.396
There's nothing, no number.


00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.433
Where is she?


00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.480
We know she lived here,
so where did she go?


00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:41.557
(Slap)


00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:42.669
Aargh!


00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.917
Where's Angela Mills?
Where did she go?


00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.075
(Slap)


00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.112
Billing, leave him.
He knows nothing.


00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.715
We're going to be late.
Go and get the car.


00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.798
(Billing) We know where you live,
where your daughter goes to school.


00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.512
Prick!


00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.355
(White) 'Another situation
needs resolving.


00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.311
'Do what you do best.


00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:21.354
'Leave no trace.'


00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:22.989
(Screaming)


00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.116
(Shouting)


00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.591
Has anyone died yet, Mr White?


00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.719
How do you plan to defend yourself?


00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.032
(Newsreader) 'RAK 295,
as has been widely reported,


00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.470
'was to be a revolutionary
over-the-counter performance enhancer.


00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.830
'As the final testing stages
were completed,


00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.394
'it slowly emerged
that serious side effects...'


00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.991
Turn that bollocks off now.


00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:00.917
- Well, what about the landlord?
- He knew nothing.


00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:02.996
- Are you sure?
- Trust me, we were thorough.


00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.315
Cooper should be
at the step-brother's house.


00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:07.874
- Who the fuck are you?
- Andy Billing, my replacement.


00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.514
- Good to meet you, sir.
- Gentlemen.


00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.436
Wait here.
Keep the bloody press out.


00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.073
Hold on a minute.


00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.908
I'm done at the end of the month, Peter.
Do you understand me? I'm done.


00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:25.510
I'm sick of dealing with all your shit
and I don't want it any more.


00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.750
We'll discuss that later.


00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:32.077
Brooke, we need to have a serious chat.


00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.911
You're not turning your back on me, too?


00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.680
This girl, the one
from the first batch of volunteers,


00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:43.916
if she turns up dead, it's prison.


00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.156
No lawsuit. Prison!


00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:47.998
She may be abroad.


00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.395
There are many
possible scenarios, Peter.


00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:52.556
We have to think positively.


00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:55.035
There's always a chance
she hasn't reacted with it.


00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:58.232
She may be immune,
may be special.


00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:01.511
- If that's the case...
- Oh, just wake up, Michael!


00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:05.792
29,999 out of 30,000 have reacted to it.


00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:08.798
That's as close to a 100% failure rate
as you're going to get!


00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:10.638
There's a message from Cooper, boss.


00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.955
If you've killed her,
there's nothing I can do.


00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.799
- Me? I told you what we should do.
- Oh, shut up!


00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:20.550
'Angela Mills is here at her step-brother's.
Can't tell what condition... Hang on.


00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:24.036
'What the fuck?
Fuck off! Go on, fuck off!


00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.354
'What do you want me to do?


00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:28.552
'Some fucking poof just got shanked.
He's bleeding all over my car.


00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:30.398
'All right, you little shit!'


00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:31.635
(Beeping)


00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:34.115
- She's at her step-brother's flat.
- Thank Christ.


00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.834
- Her condition?
- It's unknown. He's looking into it.


00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:37.949
Good.


00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.548
You, new man, go and tell Cooper
to keep his eye on her


00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.272
and get her here now.


00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:45.233
Michael, show me this mutant
that's got the press up in arms.


00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:48.158
Then I can go upstairs
and placate those bastards.


00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:49.679
Call Cooper.


00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:54.910
- Then find out what's going on.
- OK.


00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:06.315
Matt, I know I said it was over,
but I think I have to see Joe.


00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:08.795
I need to talk to him.


00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.629
You can't be serious. You said
you'd moved on from him, Angie.


00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.115
He killed a kid.
You were right to leave him.


00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.912
Well, come on.


00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:24.033
- Say something. She's your friend.
- We all know how I feel about Joe.


00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:28.439
Listen, I like Joe as well.


00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.836
Fine, I did like him.
And I know you think it was an accident.


00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.394
And if it was,
I'm sure the system will clear that up.


00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:38.477
I've got to go. My shift started at 12
and I'm already late.


00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:40.556
Just think about it.


00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:43.513
OK? Joe will always let you down.
Always.


00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:47.394
- I thought you'd support me.
- That's what I'm doing.


00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.593
I'll see you later.


00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:03.238
- Caffeine will give you arrhythmia.
- Fuck off!


00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:06.909
Seriously. Mess up your heart
like that RAK shit that's all over the news.


00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:11.714
- When's your test?
- Next week, Thursday.


00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.354
Where have you been?
It's a bloody circus here today.


00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.152
Rob's about to crack one off.


00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:18.309
Matt. Matt!


00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.357
- Where the fuck have you been?
- Told you.


00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.277
Sorry, Sergeant. Personal stuff.


00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:27.518
- How's your step-sister doing, then?
- Well, she's still confused.


00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.029
Yeah, well,
Joe's a fucking disgrace, isn't he?


00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.869
He let me down.
He let the entire MS U down.


00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.434
Anyway, listen up.
It's kicking off all over the gaff.


00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.755
Craig's taking the launch
to Battersea Bridge.


00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.872
There's some kind of riot going on.
People are diving in the drink.


00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.991
So what we're going to do


00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.270
is steam down there
and pick up the jumpers.


00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.756
So dust her down, lock 'n' load.
Let's get ready to rock 'n' roll, boys.


00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:50.869
Rob!


00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.436
- Something's wrong with Sally!
- There's always something wrong.


00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:58.314
No, she said some guy attacked her
on the way in today and she just fainted.


00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.396
I think it must be shock.


00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.112
Do I look like a fucking doctor?


00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:04.356
Oh, Jesus! Get ready!


00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.436
Come on, let's go.


00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.911
Jesus fucking Christ!


00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.957
This is John Healy, our first trialist.


00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:31.112
A week after receiving his initial dose,
he started having an allergic reaction.


00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:32.229
A bad one.


00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.873
We thought it best
to keep him in isolation.


00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:39.709
His physiology and cellular make-up
started changing two days later.


00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.949
The viral suppressants we've been
administering seemed to keep it at bay.


00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:49.276
Although it hasn't completely stopped
the abnormal changes.


00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.634
We've taken everybody off it
to see what would happen.


00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:53.749
And?


00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.309
Nothing.
He's just been lying there.


00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:59.954
Billing, that doctor.
Talk to me. What's going on?


00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:03.277
What in God's name
are these things on his back?


00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:06.676
- He's not contagious, is he?
- We're not sure.


00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.028
(Grunts)


00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:10.469
Billing, get back here.
We've got a problem.


00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:12.949
Billing, come in.


00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:16.274
(Brooke) Get an adrenaline shot. Hurry!


00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:21.589
(Sparking)


00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.470
(Brooke) Cole? Cole!


00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:28.990
- (Cole) Everybody just stay still.
- (White) What's that noise?


00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:31.429
(Trialist growls)


00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.079
(Brooke) Lockdown.


00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.519
Why are we in lockdown, Cole?


00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:47.759
(Screams)


00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.032
(White) Get me the fuck out of here!


00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:05.633
- (Trialist snarls)
- Get me out of here!


00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:19.352
Open this door!


00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.478
(Repeated shots)


00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:34.670
(Clicking)


00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:40.957
(White) What the fuck was that?
What have you done, Brooke?


00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.678
What the fuck have you done?


00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:46.073
Brooke?


00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:49.110
(Snarling)


00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:51.276
(Screams)


00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:05.391
(Snarling)


00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.233
(Crash)


00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:22.316
(Siren)


00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.117
Oi, oi!
Stay still. Stay still, will you?


00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:34.038
Stay still.
Come on, hold the crazy bastard.


00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:35.752
Come on, hold him!


00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.472
Keep fucking still, will you?


00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:41.835
Aaargh! He fucking bit me!


00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:48.310
Come on, we should go back inside.
It's not safe out here.


00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:07.992
- Where's all your cars?
- I had to get the cash from somewhere.


00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:11.795
- Fucking hell. Sorry, mate.
- Enough of that bollocks, eh?


00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:13.990
It's not important.
It's only a bit of cash.


00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:23.878
Hey, I don't think she knew
you were getting out, you know.


00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.639
I haven't seen her since I went in.


00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:28.990
No letters, no phone calls, nothing.


00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:33.950
I know I let her down.
I need to see her.


00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:37.356
- She needs to know I didn't do it.
- I wish I could help you, mate.


00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:39.675
But I haven't seen her
since it all happened.


00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:42.992
Come on, eh?


00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.995
I get 24 more hours in the air,
then I take my test.


00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:57.271
I can't wait to get off this fucking river.
It's hardly a river, is it?


00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:00.710
More like a plague-ridden cesspit
of Ebola or something.


00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:03.195
Ebola, no. Plague, maybe.


00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:05.788
- Bubonic or pneumonic?
- What's the difference?


00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.512
(Explosion)


00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:09.949
What the fuck was that?


00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.150
192 to Central, come in.


00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.793
192 to Central, come in!


00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:16.753
- Get the boat ready.
- Fucking hell!


00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:20.918
Sarge, Sarge!
Sarge, what are you doing?


00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:23.069
Sarge!


00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:26.118
Sarge, what are you doing? Guv!


00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:27.593
Guv!


00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:56.953
This is MS U Central.
We need help.


00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:58.718
Someone, come in.


00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.559
Matt, what the fuck is going on?


00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.715
(Screaming)


00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.671
This is seriously fucked up.


00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:07.951
This is MS U Central, come in.
We need help. Somebody, anybody.


00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:09.957
(Radio) 'Get out of there! Get anywhere!


00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.513
'Now!'


00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:14.279
(Voice breaks up)


00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.231
Jim, what the hell's going on?


00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.315
(Brooke) Cole?


00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.311
Cole? Cole, wake up!


00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.997
Cole!


00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:36.712
Cole, wake up!


00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:41.034
For God's sake, wake up!


00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.430
Get up, get up.


00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:06.959
Over here.


00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:14.717
Something must have gone wrong
with the code.


00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.798
What we saw is impossible.
This is just impossible.


00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.911
(Roaring)


00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:24.999
It got in behind him
as he was trying to shut the door.


00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:28.998
Well, the power's back on,
so why hasn't help arrived?


00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:31.031
I hate to think.


00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:32.878
Well, now we know it spreads.


00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:35.150
But how? Blood, maybe.


00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:39.117
Maybe saliva. I don't know.


00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:42.118
- I just don't know any more.
- So that means they've all got it.


00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:45.234
All of those upstairs


00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:47.749
and all of those in the hospitals.


00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:52.317
They're all going to catch it and
then it's going to spread even further.


00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:55.589
And now I've got it.


00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:02.673
Is there anything I can take?
The stuff you used on the other patients.


00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.997
The viral suppressant. It's in there.


00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:07.314
The syrettes.


00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:13.239
There's only three but that should
control the infection for up to 18 hours.


00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:15.351
Well, we've got to figure something out.


00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:22.834
- Aaargh!
- No, no, no!


00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:25.394
- No, no!
- Oh, shit.


00:22:25.520 --> 00:22:29.229
- I thought he was a...
- Please hang on.


00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:32.272
Cole, I didn't realise.
This place is a fucking slaughterhouse.


00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:36.154
They're all dead,
and if they're not dead, they're turning.


00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:37.269
Angela...


00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:40.278
Talk to me.
Talk to me, Michael.


00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:42.470
Find Angela Mills.


00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:46.751
(Screaming)


00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:50.350
- There's more of them coming.
- Shut up!


00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:53.439
You've been bitten.


00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:01.359
Don't.


00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:21.950
(Cole) 'I'm sick of dealing
with all your shit.


00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:25.871
'And I don't want it anymore.'


00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:37.799
(Brooke) 'Find Angela Mills.'


00:23:48.680 --> 00:23:50.318
Aaargh!


00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:23.918
(Brooke) 'There's only three but that
should control the infection for 18 hours.'


00:24:46.200 --> 00:24:47.838
(Screaming)


00:24:58.800 --> 00:24:59.755
(Car alarm)


00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:23.269
Aargh!


00:26:05.560 --> 00:26:07.198
(Tyres screech)


00:26:11.120 --> 00:26:12.712
(Growling)


00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:20.874
(TV) 'So what measures are being taken,
Clare, to combat these... things


00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:26.597
'and to calm this situation police heads
have labelled "A Devil's Playground"?'


00:26:26.720 --> 00:26:29.871
'Well, what can anyone do
to calm this situation, Adam?


00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.399
'Nobody seems to know.


00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:35.035
'The authorities are having enormous
difficulty tackling these hordes.


00:26:35.160 --> 00:26:37.355
'Their agility and strength are frightening,


00:26:37.480 --> 00:26:38.708
'truly frightening.


00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:41.593
'It seems that they will attack
anything and everything


00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:44.675
'Jesus. I think we're...


00:26:44.800 --> 00:26:47.189
'We're going to have
to come back to you, Adam.'


00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:49.632
'OK. We're hearing now...'


00:26:53.120 --> 00:26:56.829
OK, we need to get to the Abraxon
construction site in Wapping.


00:26:56.960 --> 00:26:59.349
It's by the river.
Matt and Jim will meet us there.


00:26:59.480 --> 00:27:03.189
It shouldn't take us too long.
About 40 minutes.


00:27:06.520 --> 00:27:08.556
- 'We are unable to connect your call.'
- Dead.


00:27:08.680 --> 00:27:11.399
Please, babe, let's just get out of here.
Come on.


00:27:13.560 --> 00:27:14.959
What about Joe? Shit!


00:27:15.080 --> 00:27:17.514
- What about Joe?
- He's in prison.


00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:20.837
In one of the safest places possible.
Now come on, get in the car.


00:27:39.120 --> 00:27:40.712
Please, Angie, please.


00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:47.948
You're not shitting me
about the helicopter, are you?


00:27:48.080 --> 00:27:49.798
No.


00:27:49.920 --> 00:27:52.992
My instructor goes on about
it being a silly place to have a helipad.


00:27:53.120 --> 00:27:55.634
We even flew over it the other day.


00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:57.512
The chopper's there, I swear.


00:27:57.640 --> 00:27:59.437
Just got to figure out how to get to it.


00:28:00.360 --> 00:28:01.349
Matt.


00:28:01.480 --> 00:28:05.029
There's some seriously strange noises
coming from the canteen.


00:28:05.160 --> 00:28:07.230
We need to get out of here fucking fast!


00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:12.151
Jesus Christ, we're fucked!


00:28:15.160 --> 00:28:16.559
(Steve) Yes, I know, son.


00:28:16.680 --> 00:28:20.070
That's why Mummy took you out there
with what's-his-name, isn't it?


00:28:20.200 --> 00:28:23.317
So you could enjoy Spain,
the good weather, the food.


00:28:23.440 --> 00:28:25.635
Just be a good boy for her, OK?
All right.


00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:28.274
Yes, you'll be with Daddy
in about a week, OK?


00:28:28.400 --> 00:28:31.278
All right.
I love you too, son. I miss you loads.


00:28:31.400 --> 00:28:33.356
Hey, look, put your mum on before...


00:28:35.760 --> 00:28:36.795
Great.


00:28:38.920 --> 00:28:41.878
- Did you get a doctor to look at that?
- Yeah.


00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:45.390
It might come in handy
with the trial coming up. It's proof.


00:28:50.920 --> 00:28:51.909
What the f?


00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:55.911
Someone's just done the reporter.


00:28:59.920 --> 00:29:02.388
'Er, once again, breaking news.


00:29:03.440 --> 00:29:06.910
'A state of emergency
has been declared throughout the UK.'


00:29:08.360 --> 00:29:10.430
What the fuck's going on, Joe?


00:29:13.200 --> 00:29:16.715
(TV) 'Reports are now coming in
that an infectious disease of some sort


00:29:16.840 --> 00:29:21.152
'is responsible for the outbreak
of random acts of frenzied violence.


00:29:21.280 --> 00:29:23.475
'The infected are spreading
from city centres.


00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:26.068
'If you are attacked,
the only way to stop them


00:29:26.200 --> 00:29:29.795
'appears to be with a blow
of extreme force to the head.


00:29:29.920 --> 00:29:32.514
'I repeat, the blow must be to the head.


00:29:32.640 --> 00:29:35.996
'We will be halting transmission shortly
but information will be broadcast on...'


00:29:38.480 --> 00:29:41.517
Right, we've got a couple of choices.


00:29:43.160 --> 00:29:45.799
We can either stay here,
make sure everything's secure.


00:29:45.920 --> 00:29:48.753
Or there's a fishing shed
up the road near the lake.


00:29:48.880 --> 00:29:51.394
It stinks a bit but it's made of stone
so it'll be safe.


00:29:51.520 --> 00:29:53.511
- Are you listening?
- I've got to find her.


00:29:53.640 --> 00:29:57.394
- I can't leave her out there in that mess.
- Do not do this to yourself, mate.


00:29:57.520 --> 00:30:00.318
Look, she's a clever girl.
She'll be all right.


00:30:00.440 --> 00:30:03.716
It's chaos out there.
What chance have we got of finding her?


00:30:03.840 --> 00:30:07.515
She's a smart girl. She's probably
in a safer place than we are right now.


00:30:07.640 --> 00:30:09.392
OK?


00:30:09.520 --> 00:30:13.399
So are we going to stay here
or go up to the fishing shed?


00:30:13.520 --> 00:30:14.919
Yeah.


00:30:15.040 --> 00:30:17.031
- Yeah, OK, we'll stay here.
- Right, good.


00:30:17.160 --> 00:30:20.948
You check here. I'll go out the back
and make sure everything's safe.


00:30:22.160 --> 00:30:24.276
(Car horns blare)


00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:28.188
- Matt will wait for us, won't he?
- Of course he will. He's my brother.


00:30:29.640 --> 00:30:33.155
I hate to say it, but he has got a point.
Joe's not right for you.


00:30:33.280 --> 00:30:37.478
You did so well rebuilding your life
without him. Now all that work...


00:30:37.600 --> 00:30:39.636
Kate, I've made up my mind.


00:30:39.760 --> 00:30:41.876
Have you thought
what the testing might do?


00:30:42.000 --> 00:30:45.356
No, it's fine. I'm fine.


00:30:46.360 --> 00:30:48.954
OK. Sorry. Sorry.


00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:51.992
- All this is just so fucking weird.
- I know.


00:30:52.560 --> 00:30:54.676
But we are going to be OK.


00:30:56.280 --> 00:30:58.874
Come on!
Why aren't they moving?


00:31:00.800 --> 00:31:03.678
- A345.
- What? No.


00:31:03.800 --> 00:31:06.030
That's going north.
We need to head east.


00:31:06.160 --> 00:31:09.675
It'll take us out of this bloody traffic.
We need to go out to come back in.


00:31:09.800 --> 00:31:12.189
- How?
- Come on!


00:31:15.040 --> 00:31:16.758
(Roaring)


00:31:16.880 --> 00:31:18.836
(Kate) What's going on?


00:31:18.960 --> 00:31:20.473
(Snarling)


00:31:22.800 --> 00:31:24.199
We need to get out.


00:31:28.080 --> 00:31:30.799
Hey, stop that!
What are you doing?


00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:33.399
Everybody stop!


00:31:35.120 --> 00:31:37.031
Oi! Oh, shit!


00:31:45.440 --> 00:31:48.671
(Screaming)


00:32:06.400 --> 00:32:07.469
(Snarling)


00:32:07.600 --> 00:32:09.079
Shit!


00:32:18.120 --> 00:32:20.236
(Car horns blare)


00:32:45.160 --> 00:32:46.991
(Snarling)


00:33:04.400 --> 00:33:08.234
(Radio) 'We urge all listeners in the city
to evacuate. I repeat.


00:33:08.360 --> 00:33:11.955
'Evacuate the city immediately
by any means possible.


00:33:12.080 --> 00:33:14.514
'Emergency services have been overrun.


00:33:14.640 --> 00:33:17.438
'lf any member of your group
has been bitten by the infected,


00:33:17.560 --> 00:33:19.755
'they will have limited time
before the infection


00:33:19.880 --> 00:33:21.598
'takes over their brain function.


00:33:21.720 --> 00:33:23.438
'Do not allow them to stay with you.


00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:27.519
'I repeat,
do not allow them to stay with you.'


00:33:38.160 --> 00:33:41.755
God, we're not going to make it.
We're going to have to stop somewhere.


00:33:41.880 --> 00:33:42.949
Where?


00:33:43.080 --> 00:33:44.513
Steve's.


00:33:44.640 --> 00:33:46.915
We need to try and find somewhere
with more people.


00:33:47.040 --> 00:33:48.553
Steve's is just down the road.


00:34:11.560 --> 00:34:13.915
No, no!


00:34:14.040 --> 00:34:15.632
(Engine dies)


00:34:15.760 --> 00:34:16.749
Please, not now.


00:34:16.880 --> 00:34:18.950
Not fucking now! Come on.


00:34:19.080 --> 00:34:20.399
(Car won't start)


00:34:20.520 --> 00:34:23.114
Come on!


00:34:28.400 --> 00:34:29.594
(Screeching)


00:34:33.160 --> 00:34:34.957
(Gnashing)


00:34:53.600 --> 00:34:55.795
(Angela) That's Steve's van.


00:34:55.920 --> 00:34:58.992
- (Kate) Why is it so empty?
- Something's not right.


00:35:06.400 --> 00:35:08.311
(Steve) Looks like two or three people.


00:35:18.200 --> 00:35:21.317
There's too many fucking rabbits
out there, mate.


00:35:21.440 --> 00:35:23.078
Let's get behind the bench.


00:35:55.280 --> 00:35:56.918
Hello? Oh!


00:35:58.840 --> 00:36:00.353
Ange!


00:36:00.480 --> 00:36:04.155
- What are you doing here?
- Jesus, Joe!


00:36:04.280 --> 00:36:07.317
- Why aren't you inside?
- Did you break out?


00:36:07.440 --> 00:36:08.429
What? No.


00:36:08.560 --> 00:36:12.997
Baby, I made bail.
I got out a couple of hours ago.


00:36:13.120 --> 00:36:15.190
- You're not hurt, are you?
- No, I'm fine.


00:36:15.320 --> 00:36:17.709
Well, come here.
You're safe now.


00:36:21.560 --> 00:36:24.028
You all right, Kate?


00:36:27.080 --> 00:36:28.752
So what are you doing here?


00:36:31.600 --> 00:36:32.589
Steve.


00:36:32.720 --> 00:36:35.314
Listen, the car's completely broken down.


00:36:35.440 --> 00:36:38.159
We need your help to fix it.


00:36:51.840 --> 00:36:53.239
(Steve) The radiator's gone.


00:36:53.360 --> 00:36:55.112
You won't get far like that.


00:36:55.240 --> 00:36:57.754
- Can't you lend us something?
- I haven't got anything.


00:36:57.880 --> 00:36:59.836
We had to sell the lot.
Needed the cash.


00:37:00.880 --> 00:37:03.917
You two should stay here.
We'll be all right.


00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:07.430
No, Joe, we need to get
to the Abraxon site across from MS U.


00:37:07.560 --> 00:37:10.472
Matt's meeting us there with Jim.
Jim's learning to be a pilot.


00:37:10.600 --> 00:37:12.670
He says they've got a helicopter.


00:37:13.440 --> 00:37:15.715
So what are you doing here?
Wapping's the other way.


00:37:15.840 --> 00:37:18.638
- We figured we'd go round the traffic.
- Who's Jim?


00:37:20.520 --> 00:37:23.478
- Jim's got your old job.
- Kate!


00:37:23.600 --> 00:37:24.589
Fuck 'em.


00:37:24.720 --> 00:37:27.393
As far as they're concerned,
I'm fucking guilty.


00:37:27.520 --> 00:37:30.398
Did you think they were going
to give you your job back?


00:37:30.520 --> 00:37:31.999
No, we're safe here.


00:37:32.880 --> 00:37:34.916
- Joe...
- The news says to stay indoors.


00:37:35.040 --> 00:37:36.519
In all fairness, it did say that.


00:37:36.640 --> 00:37:39.108
You'd be stupid to go into town.
It's carnage out there.


00:37:39.240 --> 00:37:41.037
The news said it was pretty fucking bad.


00:37:41.160 --> 00:37:42.593
Well, this is hardly Fort Knox!


00:37:44.280 --> 00:37:47.033
How do we know
Matt and Jim will even be there?


00:37:47.160 --> 00:37:48.878
Unlike you, Joe, we can trust them.


00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:50.319
- What?
- You know what.


00:37:50.440 --> 00:37:52.112
Just hang on for a minute.


00:37:54.360 --> 00:37:55.873
(Rattling)


00:37:56.000 --> 00:37:57.718
- (Kate) Ange!
- Get the gun!


00:37:58.720 --> 00:37:59.948
(Kate) What the fuck is it?


00:38:00.080 --> 00:38:02.275
No, no, no!


00:38:04.040 --> 00:38:06.270
(Rattling)


00:38:11.600 --> 00:38:13.989
(Man) Don't shoot!
(Woman) Get away from the door!


00:38:15.840 --> 00:38:18.798
- (American accent) Easy, easy!
- Now just calm down, all right?


00:38:18.920 --> 00:38:21.912
Just calm down.


00:38:31.200 --> 00:38:33.031
(Kate) What the fuck is that?


00:38:33.160 --> 00:38:35.833
(Girls wail)


00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:13.151
There you go, mate.
Do you want one, love?


00:39:13.280 --> 00:39:14.918
- No, thanks.
- Fair enough.


00:39:15.040 --> 00:39:18.794
So glad just to see
some normal faces, you know.


00:39:18.920 --> 00:39:20.751
What's going on?
What happened?


00:39:20.880 --> 00:39:24.031
Er, well,
we were on our way to work


00:39:24.160 --> 00:39:25.718
Near Bank.


00:39:25.840 --> 00:39:29.071
My colleague, Alex Johnson,
that's the guy who tried to...


00:39:29.200 --> 00:39:30.599
That was him.


00:39:31.560 --> 00:39:33.357
He was travelling with us


00:39:33.480 --> 00:39:36.119
when the subway stopped
and all the lights went out.


00:39:36.240 --> 00:39:38.800
The emergency lights came on.
The screaming had started.


00:39:39.600 --> 00:39:43.878
(Man) They came through the carriages,
clambering over each other like insects.


00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:47.754
They bite you. It's like, they bite you
and then you become one of them.


00:39:47.880 --> 00:39:52.556
So we ran through the tunnels
till we got back to the station.


00:39:52.680 --> 00:39:55.638
- The police couldn't do much.
- No, they did nothing.


00:39:56.400 --> 00:39:59.233
One cop, I mean, he had a shotgun.


00:39:59.360 --> 00:40:01.396
He'd been bitten three or four times.


00:40:01.520 --> 00:40:05.433
So he turned...
He turned the gun around.


00:40:07.200 --> 00:40:10.351
- His head split open like a log.
- (Joe) Fucking Jesus!


00:40:10.480 --> 00:40:12.596
Well, that settles it.


00:40:12.720 --> 00:40:15.553
We barricade these fucking doors
and we stay here.


00:40:15.680 --> 00:40:18.353
No, wait a second.
You haven't understood.


00:40:18.480 --> 00:40:21.074
These things chase people.
That's all they care about.


00:40:22.840 --> 00:40:25.593
Everybody's running away from the city.


00:40:25.720 --> 00:40:27.915
Running this way.


00:40:28.040 --> 00:40:31.430
(Kate) Do you hear that?
There can't be any questions now.


00:40:31.560 --> 00:40:34.597
We go to the Abraxon site, yeah?


00:40:34.720 --> 00:40:36.995
- What's there?
- (Steve) There's a helicopter.


00:40:37.120 --> 00:40:40.032
- (Man) Sounds like a plan.
- (Joe) Why don't we head for the coast?


00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:41.559
There's too many of us.


00:40:42.600 --> 00:40:45.637
There's not enough room.
Matt said it was a four-seater helicopter.


00:40:45.760 --> 00:40:48.115
(Joe) Four people.
It's a fucking joke!


00:40:49.160 --> 00:40:51.833
No, we'll make it work.
We'll make it work somehow.


00:41:18.680 --> 00:41:20.636
Oh, my God.
There's someone outside.


00:41:21.920 --> 00:41:22.909
Joe!


00:41:33.080 --> 00:41:35.196
Aaaargh!


00:41:55.200 --> 00:41:56.428
(Screeching)


00:42:03.920 --> 00:42:04.909
(Snarling)


00:42:12.920 --> 00:42:15.673
Is he one of them?


00:42:15.800 --> 00:42:17.870
You all right, mate?


00:42:21.600 --> 00:42:22.396
(Breaking glass)


00:42:22.520 --> 00:42:25.080
Shit, they're coming
through the office window!


00:42:25.200 --> 00:42:26.189
Fuck it!


00:42:30.840 --> 00:42:32.239
Get over there!


00:42:40.880 --> 00:42:41.949
Take this.


00:42:42.080 --> 00:42:43.195
(Roaring)


00:42:47.320 --> 00:42:49.629
(Snarling)


00:42:50.760 --> 00:42:54.719
On three, you go over the top
and you go behind me, OK?


00:42:58.760 --> 00:42:59.749
One...


00:43:01.280 --> 00:43:02.076
two...


00:43:03.440 --> 00:43:04.634
three!


00:43:28.040 --> 00:43:29.029
(Girls scream)


00:43:35.240 --> 00:43:37.117
(Sobbing)


00:44:13.400 --> 00:44:14.879
Matt, wait.


00:44:15.000 --> 00:44:16.911
Sandra, what?


00:44:17.040 --> 00:44:18.598
Sandra?


00:44:18.720 --> 00:44:21.359
- (Choking)
- (Jim) Oh, Jesus! Sandra?


00:44:27.200 --> 00:44:28.269
(Sandra) Run!


00:44:29.920 --> 00:44:31.433
No, Andy!


00:44:31.560 --> 00:44:32.959
Fuck!


00:44:33.080 --> 00:44:34.877
Fucking hell, run!


00:44:35.000 --> 00:44:36.433
Run! Run!


00:44:36.920 --> 00:44:37.909
(Snarling)


00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:42.275
(Jim screams)


00:45:10.600 --> 00:45:12.989
Jim, look.
They're scared of the water.


00:45:14.800 --> 00:45:17.758
We might make it, Jim.
We might just fucking make it.


00:45:20.200 --> 00:45:23.237
Jesus Christ, are you OK?


00:45:24.440 --> 00:45:26.078
Keep it raised.


00:45:26.200 --> 00:45:29.875
- Let's just get out of here. I'll be fine.
- Try and stop the blood flow.


00:45:38.960 --> 00:45:41.349
(Wailing)


00:45:46.680 --> 00:45:48.033
Ow!


00:45:51.400 --> 00:45:53.834
That's all we can do.
We were quick. You might be lucky.


00:45:55.360 --> 00:45:58.318
- What about me?
- What about you?


00:46:00.720 --> 00:46:02.119
I'm still here, ain't I?


00:46:04.360 --> 00:46:05.759
All right, listen, everyone.


00:46:06.800 --> 00:46:10.475
You've seen what two of them can do.
They move fast and they spread fast.


00:46:10.600 --> 00:46:12.397
We need to do exactly the same thing.


00:46:12.880 --> 00:46:15.633
Now, as this is a garage,
I'm hoping there's a car we can use.


00:46:15.760 --> 00:46:17.352
Who are you?


00:46:18.520 --> 00:46:20.238
(Joe) She asked you a question.


00:46:21.600 --> 00:46:23.989
- I'm Cole.
- (Angela) What are you doing?


00:46:24.120 --> 00:46:26.190
I'm running, just like everyone else.


00:46:26.320 --> 00:46:28.788
We're all in the same boat
so we need to help each other.


00:46:28.920 --> 00:46:31.480
What happened back there?
Looked like a heart attack.


00:46:31.600 --> 00:46:33.318
What are you, a fucking doctor?


00:46:35.760 --> 00:46:37.955
I'm a diabetic.


00:46:38.080 --> 00:46:40.719
There's a van outside.
I need to change the fuel pump.


00:46:40.840 --> 00:46:42.717
I think I can use
the one from Angie's car.


00:46:42.840 --> 00:46:44.751
I'll try and make a start on it, all right?


00:46:48.920 --> 00:46:51.036
There's a helicopter
at a site in Wapping.


00:46:51.160 --> 00:46:54.675
Yeah, but that's that way, isn't it?
Back in the shit.


00:46:54.800 --> 00:46:56.438
Don't see your helicopter outside.


00:46:58.960 --> 00:47:01.872
- OK, so what type is it?
- I don't know. It's a four-seater.


00:47:02.000 --> 00:47:05.436
Well, the only way round that
is to do multiple trips.


00:47:05.560 --> 00:47:07.755
I'm good with cars
but not with helicopters.


00:47:07.880 --> 00:47:09.438
(Angela) We have a pilot.


00:47:10.520 --> 00:47:12.078
And who would that be?


00:47:12.200 --> 00:47:14.270
He's a friend of ours.
He's meeting us there.


00:47:15.080 --> 00:47:16.991
I need a map. Show me.


00:47:19.480 --> 00:47:21.710
And now there's even more of us.


00:47:29.440 --> 00:47:33.115
(Cole) Steve, you've got to be quick.
There's not a lot of time.


00:47:35.600 --> 00:47:38.353
Have you got any soya milk?


00:47:38.480 --> 00:47:40.675
Yeah, it'll be in the fridge
next to the caviar.


00:47:44.480 --> 00:47:47.040
The man in the suit,
is that the policeman that?


00:47:47.160 --> 00:47:50.869
- Yeah, that's the same prick.
- Hey, Katie, watch your mouth, eh?


00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:54.072
- He's still a good mate of mine.
- I'm sorry, I'm just...


00:47:54.200 --> 00:47:56.156
I'm not coping well with this, you know?


00:47:56.280 --> 00:47:59.716
Yeah, well, the way I see it,
everybody deserves a second chance.


00:48:08.120 --> 00:48:09.712
It is him.


00:48:11.440 --> 00:48:13.192
Yeah, I thought so.


00:48:13.800 --> 00:48:16.075
He was meant
to go on trial sometime soon.


00:48:17.120 --> 00:48:18.997
Shot a kid who stole a boat.


00:48:21.000 --> 00:48:24.231
Back home a cock-sucker gets the chair,
no questions asked.


00:48:25.840 --> 00:48:28.479
There's something
that's bothering me more than that.


00:48:28.600 --> 00:48:31.797
- What's that?
- Friends and family.


00:48:31.920 --> 00:48:34.388
Most important thing in the world.


00:48:34.520 --> 00:48:35.999
And we're neither.


00:48:38.120 --> 00:48:39.792
We're the outsiders here.


00:48:42.280 --> 00:48:46.671
OK, the helicopter holds four people.
So we do three separate trips as agreed.


00:48:48.720 --> 00:48:50.551
I'll go last.


00:48:52.000 --> 00:48:55.231
- You all right, mate?
- I didn't agree to it.


00:48:55.360 --> 00:48:57.874
- It's a fucked-up plan.
- Why?


00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:01.879
What if the pilot don't want to come back
or the chopper runs out of juice?


00:49:02.000 --> 00:49:03.831
What do the second and third parties do?


00:49:03.960 --> 00:49:07.032
Just wait around and be attacked?
Forget the helicopter.


00:49:07.160 --> 00:49:08.513
We drive.


00:49:08.640 --> 00:49:11.029
We go to Dover, Folkestone, wherever.
We grab a boat.


00:49:11.160 --> 00:49:13.515
Are you mad?
You'd last ten minutes at the most.


00:49:13.640 --> 00:49:17.030
I've just spent two months in prison.
I think I can handle a road.


00:49:17.160 --> 00:49:19.515
Yeah, well, once we get the helicopter,


00:49:19.640 --> 00:49:22.154
you're more than welcome
to the van and the road.


00:49:22.920 --> 00:49:25.798
Me and Angela will drop you at
the Abraxon place and then go our...


00:49:25.920 --> 00:49:29.151
You go on your own.
She comes with us.


00:49:29.280 --> 00:49:32.397
Are you fucking serious?
What, you think I'm some sort of?


00:49:32.520 --> 00:49:33.919
Jesus, enough!


00:49:36.120 --> 00:49:38.236
She stays with me.


00:49:38.360 --> 00:49:39.918
Do you understand?


00:49:47.760 --> 00:49:50.513
How long with that fuel pump?
We've got to get that van going.


00:49:51.160 --> 00:49:52.673
(Groaning)


00:50:01.920 --> 00:50:04.514
How's your arm, Jim?
Is it getting worse?


00:50:05.400 --> 00:50:06.879
Look, whatever "it" is,


00:50:07.000 --> 00:50:09.036
Andy's infected me with it.


00:50:09.160 --> 00:50:10.195
Fucking arsehole!


00:50:12.880 --> 00:50:14.552
If we don't make it to the helipad,


00:50:14.680 --> 00:50:16.238
just fucking throw me overboard.


00:50:16.360 --> 00:50:17.429
I'm not doing that, Jim.


00:50:17.560 --> 00:50:21.553
You can't let me
become one of those things.


00:50:21.680 --> 00:50:23.079
I can't do that, Jim.


00:50:29.120 --> 00:50:30.519
OK.


00:50:31.840 --> 00:50:33.273
Promise me.


00:50:35.000 --> 00:50:35.989
I promise.


00:51:09.600 --> 00:51:11.955
Why are you showing me this?


00:51:14.640 --> 00:51:16.710
- You know why.
- I'm fine.


00:51:17.280 --> 00:51:19.316
I'm absolutely fine.


00:51:19.440 --> 00:51:21.192
That's why I'm here.


00:51:21.320 --> 00:51:22.958
Because of the testing.


00:51:23.080 --> 00:51:26.709
Everyone who took RAK
has turned into one of those things.


00:51:26.840 --> 00:51:29.149
I saw one change
right in front of my own eyes.


00:51:30.360 --> 00:51:34.911
- Are you saying that I'm next?
- No, I don't think you will be.


00:51:36.160 --> 00:51:39.675
30,000 people turned
and are spreading it.


00:51:39.800 --> 00:51:43.110
For some reason,
you're different from all the other trialists.


00:51:43.240 --> 00:51:45.515
You're special somehow.


00:51:45.640 --> 00:51:48.871
We've got to get you
out the country and into a lab.


00:51:49.000 --> 00:51:50.797
And we've got to do some tests.


00:51:51.600 --> 00:51:55.275
You might be the person to stop all this,
but first things first.


00:51:55.400 --> 00:51:57.197
You listen to me.


00:52:06.560 --> 00:52:08.710
Just leave me alone, Joe.


00:52:15.360 --> 00:52:17.749
That shit on TV.


00:52:19.080 --> 00:52:21.355
It's the reason behind all this.


00:52:22.080 --> 00:52:24.992
People having heart problems.


00:52:25.120 --> 00:52:27.395
They're the symptoms,


00:52:27.520 --> 00:52:29.078
the start of it.


00:52:32.240 --> 00:52:34.515
I was one of the first trialists.


00:52:38.160 --> 00:52:39.957
- So are you?
- No.


00:52:41.120 --> 00:52:43.190
I haven't got any symptoms.


00:52:44.320 --> 00:52:46.436
I'm the only one who hasn't.


00:52:49.200 --> 00:52:52.237
- Why did you do it?
- Why do you think, Joe?


00:52:53.200 --> 00:52:56.078
I was trying to rebuild my life.


00:52:56.200 --> 00:52:58.316
I needed the money.


00:52:58.440 --> 00:53:00.476
Who told you about the drug?


00:53:01.240 --> 00:53:02.958
Cole?


00:53:05.400 --> 00:53:08.756
He's lying.
Doesn't make sense.


00:53:08.880 --> 00:53:11.713
- Why is it spreading?
- I don't want to talk about it anymore.


00:53:11.840 --> 00:53:13.592
I don't want to talk about it, Joe.


00:53:26.640 --> 00:53:28.676
In all the time we were together,


00:53:30.800 --> 00:53:32.995
I never lied to you once, Ange.


00:53:35.280 --> 00:53:37.316
I just want you to know that.


00:53:41.080 --> 00:53:42.672
I'm pregnant, Joe.


00:53:44.200 --> 00:53:45.713
What?


00:54:27.800 --> 00:54:30.030
Well, do you want to keep it?


00:54:31.560 --> 00:54:34.233
Yeah. I think I do.


00:54:48.360 --> 00:54:49.759
I'll be there for you.


00:54:51.600 --> 00:54:54.592
You know that, don't you?
No matter what.


00:54:55.400 --> 00:54:58.119
All the more reason
to get you out of here in one piece, eh?


00:55:08.080 --> 00:55:09.433
Steve's nearly done.


00:55:09.560 --> 00:55:10.709
We need to move. Now.


00:55:12.160 --> 00:55:13.559
For fuck's sake.


00:55:13.680 --> 00:55:15.955
- What are you doing?
- Sorry.


00:55:16.080 --> 00:55:18.674
- Just practising.
- Practising what?


00:55:18.800 --> 00:55:20.358
Give me the weapon.


00:55:20.480 --> 00:55:22.516
- Stand up.
- Why?


00:55:22.640 --> 00:55:25.518
- Stand up!
- Hey, come on.


00:55:25.640 --> 00:55:27.710
Let me tell you something.


00:55:27.840 --> 00:55:31.037
Right here, right now,
you do exactly as I say.


00:55:31.160 --> 00:55:34.277
And don't fucking question me again.
You got that?


00:55:37.160 --> 00:55:40.072
- Show me your hand.
- (Woman) You be careful!


00:55:45.960 --> 00:55:47.552
Am I going to be OK?


00:55:49.440 --> 00:55:50.429
Probably.


00:55:51.280 --> 00:55:54.750
- What do you mean, "probably"?
- You ready?


00:55:54.880 --> 00:55:56.916
- I'm coming as well.
- Whatever.


00:55:58.320 --> 00:55:59.309
Geoff.


00:56:00.440 --> 00:56:02.670
He's going to leave us behind.


00:56:02.800 --> 00:56:06.315
That's exactly what's going to happen.
He doesn't like us.


00:56:06.440 --> 00:56:09.432
If there are too many of us
and not enough room on that helicopter,


00:56:09.560 --> 00:56:11.994
- we're the ones he'll leave.
- Yeah, but Lavinia...


00:56:12.120 --> 00:56:15.795
- Geoffrey.
- We won't let that happen.


00:56:18.360 --> 00:56:20.032
Right?


00:56:43.680 --> 00:56:45.671
(Joe) There's something
I want you to know.


00:56:46.200 --> 00:56:47.599
Yeah?


00:56:47.720 --> 00:56:49.995
She's pregnant and it's mine.


00:56:50.920 --> 00:56:54.037
So whether she's immune or not,
she's coming with me.


00:56:54.160 --> 00:56:57.675
There's no way I'm letting them
become someone's chemistry project.


00:56:59.640 --> 00:57:01.631
So you'd better stay
out of my fucking way.


00:57:05.800 --> 00:57:07.950
You know, there was a time


00:57:08.080 --> 00:57:11.834
when right now you'd be screaming
and begging for mercy.


00:57:20.320 --> 00:57:22.117
The RAK testing, Katie.


00:57:22.240 --> 00:57:25.437
It's responsible for all of this.


00:57:25.560 --> 00:57:28.632
- You don't know that.
- I do know that.


00:57:28.760 --> 00:57:29.749
Cole told me.


00:57:29.880 --> 00:57:33.429
He works at N-gen.
He saw a guy who took it there turn.


00:57:34.440 --> 00:57:35.793
What?


00:57:35.920 --> 00:57:37.911
God, I don't know. I don't know.


00:57:38.920 --> 00:57:39.909
I'm so scared.


00:57:40.040 --> 00:57:42.110
Oh, my God.


00:57:42.240 --> 00:57:44.993
You could turn into one of those things.


00:57:46.160 --> 00:57:47.991
What?


00:57:48.120 --> 00:57:49.792
No, I won't.


00:57:49.920 --> 00:57:52.639
I'm fine. I'm fine right now.


00:57:53.600 --> 00:57:54.635
Yeah, sorry.


00:57:54.760 --> 00:57:56.671
I'm shocked, that's all.


00:57:59.000 --> 00:58:01.036
You've said all along
you feel fine, right?


00:58:02.880 --> 00:58:04.074
Right?


00:58:08.880 --> 00:58:10.996
Fuck!


00:58:20.200 --> 00:58:21.918
(Sighs)


00:58:23.440 --> 00:58:24.714
Hey.


00:58:28.280 --> 00:58:30.999
You know, in the States RAK 295


00:58:31.120 --> 00:58:34.271
was apparently going
to be marketed as Quentinium.


00:58:35.000 --> 00:58:36.991
So?


00:58:37.120 --> 00:58:39.270
Lucky nobody in here takes it, that's all.


00:58:39.400 --> 00:58:41.550
Imagine if they did. My God!


00:58:41.680 --> 00:58:42.669
She's fine.


00:58:42.800 --> 00:58:45.075
You're the one with the bitten finger,
remember?


00:58:45.200 --> 00:58:48.158
Come on, Kate.
Do I look dangerous to you?


00:58:48.280 --> 00:58:50.111
If that crap had got into my bloodstream,


00:58:50.240 --> 00:58:51.832
do you think I'd be sitting here?


00:58:51.960 --> 00:58:54.428
Yeah, well, Ange is not exactly
biting people, is she?


00:58:54.560 --> 00:58:56.949
Yeah, but I'm not the one
who's been injected with RAK.


00:58:59.360 --> 00:59:02.830
- She could be immune.
- Well, are you willing to take that risk?


00:59:04.320 --> 00:59:06.117
I can't help but wonder
what would happen


00:59:06.240 --> 00:59:09.550
if we're halfway across the Channel
in that chopper with nowhere to go


00:59:09.680 --> 00:59:12.478
and she turns into one of those things.


00:59:12.600 --> 00:59:14.033
What then?


00:59:15.480 --> 00:59:17.755
I know it's not an easy thing
to imagine, Kate,


00:59:17.880 --> 00:59:20.758
your friend becoming
like one of those things.


00:59:20.880 --> 00:59:22.996
But the same thing happened
to my colleague


00:59:23.120 --> 00:59:24.599
and it's no longer them.


00:59:25.560 --> 00:59:27.357
They're as good as dead.


00:59:29.160 --> 00:59:30.559
Actually, they're worse.


00:59:33.960 --> 00:59:35.837
What? Tell me. What?


00:59:35.960 --> 00:59:37.359
You know what?


00:59:37.480 --> 00:59:39.152
I want you to get out of the car.


00:59:39.960 --> 00:59:42.793
- Get out of the car!
- Hey, it's just an opinion, all right?


00:59:49.160 --> 00:59:50.309
Lavie,


00:59:52.280 --> 00:59:54.669
the blonde,


00:59:54.800 --> 00:59:59.237
she's infected with the same shit
that turns you into one of those things.


00:59:59.360 --> 01:00:01.157
That's all we need.


01:00:10.320 --> 01:00:11.719
Sorted.


01:00:15.480 --> 01:00:17.357
(Car won't start)


01:00:22.000 --> 01:00:23.752
What is it?


01:00:28.800 --> 01:00:32.031
We have to move, now.
Everybody get moving!


01:00:35.440 --> 01:00:37.670
- Joe?
- Get the flashlights from the office.


01:00:38.720 --> 01:00:40.950
OK, now's our chance. Lock her in!


01:00:44.760 --> 01:00:46.512
- Lavie!
- Close the fucking door!


01:00:53.000 --> 01:00:54.069
Katie?


01:00:54.200 --> 01:00:55.189
Katie!


01:00:55.320 --> 01:00:57.834
All right, let's go.
Let's move! Get out of here!


01:00:58.600 --> 01:01:00.272
- The van won't start, mate.
- Angela?


01:01:06.000 --> 01:01:09.788
(Growling)


01:01:09.920 --> 01:01:13.708
(Steve) Wait, I can't get the van started.
Into the woods, move!


01:01:13.840 --> 01:01:15.432
Move! Move it!


01:01:17.560 --> 01:01:18.754
(Growls)


01:01:42.240 --> 01:01:43.275
(Snarls)


01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:47.389
(Tyres screech)


01:02:26.960 --> 01:02:29.235
- What happened?
- I don't know.


01:02:29.360 --> 01:02:32.352
A shelf fell across the door.
I was trapped. We have to find them.


01:02:32.480 --> 01:02:34.789
- Baby, they could be anywhere.
- What? No...


01:02:34.920 --> 01:02:37.480
We need to think about other things.
Let's get to the coast.


01:02:37.600 --> 01:02:40.319
No, please, we have to.


01:02:43.080 --> 01:02:45.116
I think there's one place we can try.


01:02:55.760 --> 01:02:57.239
Abraxon, Jim.


01:02:57.360 --> 01:02:59.032
We made it. We're here.


01:02:59.160 --> 01:03:00.559
Grab it, grab it!


01:03:00.680 --> 01:03:02.716
(Jim groans)


01:03:11.600 --> 01:03:12.953
Jim.


01:03:13.080 --> 01:03:15.150
Jim, OK.


01:03:15.280 --> 01:03:18.317
I'm going to go and have a look
and then I'll come back for you.


01:03:18.440 --> 01:03:20.715
- OK?
- Yes. Just hurry up, will you?


01:03:21.320 --> 01:03:23.072
Or I won't be able to fly anything.


01:03:28.680 --> 01:03:30.511
And Matt...


01:03:32.400 --> 01:03:35.915
Remember what I said, yeah? Before.


01:03:54.800 --> 01:03:56.916
Angie?


01:04:47.960 --> 01:04:48.949
Aaaargh!


01:05:42.760 --> 01:05:46.639
(Geoff) Are you kidding? A fishing hut!
(Steve) You got any better ideas?


01:05:46.760 --> 01:05:48.352
No, I didn't think so.


01:05:48.480 --> 01:05:52.029
Joe knows where this place is.
So this is where he'll come, all right?


01:05:52.160 --> 01:05:53.991
- Are you sure he'll come?
- Joe's a mate.


01:05:54.120 --> 01:05:55.997
We still don't know where Ange is.


01:05:56.120 --> 01:05:58.793
Let's get inside here and wait for Joe.
He knows where we are.


01:06:13.480 --> 01:06:14.913
Aaargh!


01:06:16.600 --> 01:06:18.158
Katie!


01:06:18.280 --> 01:06:20.191
(Snarling)


01:06:49.200 --> 01:06:52.431
Oh, my God. Oh, my God!


01:06:52.560 --> 01:06:55.393
Oh, my God, Steve, I'm so sorry.


01:06:55.520 --> 01:06:56.839
I'm so sorry!


01:06:56.960 --> 01:07:00.350
Let us in, you fucking bastards!
Let us in!


01:07:02.480 --> 01:07:03.674
Ange.


01:07:03.800 --> 01:07:05.552
You can't do what Cole says.


01:07:06.440 --> 01:07:08.158
He'll take you to some fucked-up lab.


01:07:09.800 --> 01:07:11.791
They'll do
all sorts of experiments on you.


01:07:12.800 --> 01:07:14.631
They may even force you
to lose the baby.


01:07:17.840 --> 01:07:21.116
Joe, what really happened
on the boat with that kid?


01:07:32.960 --> 01:07:35.394
I replay that moment in my mind
every single day.


01:07:37.880 --> 01:07:39.472
Sometimes...


01:07:41.240 --> 01:07:43.435
I manage to talk sense into him,
you know?


01:07:46.040 --> 01:07:47.996
I manage to get the gun off him,


01:07:49.600 --> 01:07:51.989
and then I'm the hero.


01:07:52.120 --> 01:07:55.715
The hero who saved a young man
high on crack from shooting someone.


01:07:57.200 --> 01:07:59.589
And not the cop
who killed a 14-year-old kid.


01:08:04.400 --> 01:08:07.312
It doesn't matter now. He's dead.


01:08:09.320 --> 01:08:11.914
And whether he deserved it or not,
I helped him on his way.


01:08:14.680 --> 01:08:17.478
That's something I'll have to live with
for the rest of my life.


01:08:18.640 --> 01:08:20.835
I'm not going to let you down again.


01:08:33.160 --> 01:08:35.674
Open the fucking door!


01:08:38.000 --> 01:08:39.638
Fuck. Fuck!


01:08:41.840 --> 01:08:43.398
We're nearly there.


01:08:44.160 --> 01:08:46.071
Once she's gone,
there's only four of us.


01:08:47.600 --> 01:08:48.589
I can't do this.


01:08:48.720 --> 01:08:49.869
What are you doing?


01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:52.434
Hey, you listen to me!
We have to open the door.


01:08:52.560 --> 01:08:54.755
She will attract more of those things.


01:08:54.880 --> 01:08:56.313
Is that what you want?


01:08:56.440 --> 01:08:57.919
Huh?


01:09:00.400 --> 01:09:01.992
- Kate, I'm sorry...
- How could you?


01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:04.395
- What was I meant to do?
- What is the matter with you?


01:09:04.520 --> 01:09:05.953
Leave him alone!


01:09:06.080 --> 01:09:07.479
You fucking bitch!


01:09:08.920 --> 01:09:10.319
You fucking bitch!


01:09:10.440 --> 01:09:12.192
Angie!


01:09:13.880 --> 01:09:15.472
Those fuckers locked us out.


01:09:15.600 --> 01:09:17.750
(Geoff) Hey, we were attacked.


01:09:18.920 --> 01:09:20.717
(Cole) You know what'll happen to him.


01:09:21.960 --> 01:09:22.949
Fuck off!


01:09:23.080 --> 01:09:25.389
She's staying with me.


01:09:25.520 --> 01:09:28.592
She don't want to go with you.
I'm not going to tell you again.


01:09:29.520 --> 01:09:31.636
You really think it's that easy?


01:09:31.760 --> 01:09:33.876
Don't fucking tell me...


01:09:35.080 --> 01:09:37.196
- I can if I have to.
- No, you can't.


01:09:38.280 --> 01:09:41.795
Because I can tell
you ain't got it in you, Joe.


01:09:41.920 --> 01:09:43.353
I can see it in your eyes.


01:09:45.600 --> 01:09:48.194
Because I've killed more people
than I care to remember


01:09:48.320 --> 01:09:53.599
and I do not want to see you
ever, ever end up like me.


01:10:01.840 --> 01:10:02.829
Listen to me.


01:10:06.360 --> 01:10:07.349
Take that to him.


01:10:11.880 --> 01:10:13.279
Do it.


01:10:29.200 --> 01:10:31.236
(Kate) Oh, fuck!


01:10:34.120 --> 01:10:35.314
Joe.


01:10:37.400 --> 01:10:39.789
I don't want my little boy to know


01:10:43.400 --> 01:10:45.391
I knew you'd come back, mate.


01:11:10.560 --> 01:11:11.959
(Gunshot)


01:11:19.360 --> 01:11:20.270
You.


01:11:21.560 --> 01:11:24.358
What did I say to you?
What did I say to you?


01:11:24.480 --> 01:11:27.040
- He hasn't done anything.
- Shut your fucking mouth!


01:11:27.160 --> 01:11:31.676
- Stay away.
- You two are staying here.


01:11:32.560 --> 01:11:34.039
How's your back, Angela?


01:11:34.840 --> 01:11:35.875
Huh?


01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:37.399
How's that chest pain?


01:11:38.280 --> 01:11:41.829
She took RAK. She's going to turn
into one of those fucking things.


01:11:41.960 --> 01:11:45.032
Get on your fucking knees!
You left her in there, didn't you?


01:11:45.160 --> 01:11:48.436
- You left her in there. Answer me.
- He didn't do anything!


01:11:48.560 --> 01:11:52.439
- She did!
- What? That's not true.


01:11:53.920 --> 01:11:55.194
That's a lie.


01:11:55.320 --> 01:11:56.958
I didn't do anything.


01:11:57.080 --> 01:11:58.798
That's a fucking lie!


01:11:59.800 --> 01:12:01.995
Don't, Cole. It isn't right.


01:12:02.120 --> 01:12:06.272
She knows you're going to turn
into one of them. She doesn't trust you.


01:12:06.400 --> 01:12:07.469
None of us do.


01:12:08.000 --> 01:12:10.230
(Kate) Please, I didn't do anything.


01:12:10.360 --> 01:12:12.510
I promise you, I didn't do anything!


01:12:12.640 --> 01:12:14.631
Please believe me.


01:12:17.560 --> 01:12:19.312
That's just it, though, isn't it?


01:12:20.200 --> 01:12:21.599
You just left me there.


01:12:21.720 --> 01:12:25.269
You didn't try to help me.
You did nothing.


01:12:25.400 --> 01:12:27.038
Everyone in the van.


01:12:27.160 --> 01:12:29.310
- (Cole) Hold on.
- I don't care what you think!


01:12:30.320 --> 01:12:32.072
I'm not lowering myself to their level.


01:12:54.640 --> 01:12:56.631
(Police radio)


01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:01.911
Matthew Mills
of the Marine Support Unit.


01:13:02.040 --> 01:13:03.917
Come in, HMS Valiant.


01:13:04.040 --> 01:13:08.477
'This is HMS Valiant. Five miles east
from city limits along the River Thames.


01:13:08.600 --> 01:13:12.559
'Any surviving citizens are to proceed
water-bound eastward along the Thames


01:13:12.680 --> 01:13:14.432
'and await rescue. Over.'


01:13:15.800 --> 01:13:19.679
Proceed eastbound
along the Thames on the water. Copy.


01:13:19.800 --> 01:13:22.439
Copy that. We'll be there. Wait for us!


01:13:22.560 --> 01:13:24.710
'Proceed water-bound eastward, Mills.


01:13:24.840 --> 01:13:27.400
'We will remain in situ for 12 hours. Over.'


01:13:27.520 --> 01:13:29.511
Copy that.
We'll be there, we'll be there.


01:13:33.440 --> 01:13:34.839
Angie!


01:13:41.360 --> 01:13:42.759
Jim?


01:13:47.560 --> 01:13:48.879
(Grunts)


01:13:49.000 --> 01:13:51.753
It's me, Matt.
Come on, it's Matt.


01:13:51.880 --> 01:13:53.029
What is it, mate? What?


01:13:53.920 --> 01:13:55.638
Stop.


01:13:56.560 --> 01:13:58.039
Jim.


01:14:01.280 --> 01:14:03.271
Jim. Jim!


01:14:03.400 --> 01:14:04.913
Jim, listen to me.
Listen to me.


01:14:05.040 --> 01:14:06.996
(Growls)


01:14:20.560 --> 01:14:23.313
(Snarling)


01:14:56.440 --> 01:14:58.237
What if it happens
when we're in the air?


01:14:58.360 --> 01:15:00.476
- What then?
- Why don't you shut up?


01:15:00.600 --> 01:15:03.273
- Am I the only one concerned?
- (Cole) How's your hand?


01:15:05.040 --> 01:15:06.029
It's stopped hurting.


01:15:06.160 --> 01:15:07.718
- Has it?
- Yes.


01:15:07.840 --> 01:15:09.751
- It has.
- Good.


01:15:09.880 --> 01:15:10.949
Stop the van.


01:15:11.080 --> 01:15:13.640
- What?
- Stop the van, Cole!


01:15:16.840 --> 01:15:18.751
I'm not going.


01:15:18.880 --> 01:15:22.111
- You're forgetting something.
- The real monsters are in this van.


01:15:22.240 --> 01:15:24.356
- I know that.
- They can have their helicopter.


01:15:24.480 --> 01:15:28.393
I'll take my chances on the road with Joe.
I can't stop those things getting to us.


01:15:28.520 --> 01:15:30.476
But I can stop this lot.


01:15:30.600 --> 01:15:33.160
- They would rather see me dead.
- Now you listen to me.


01:15:33.800 --> 01:15:35.279
I've got you this far, haven't I?


01:15:36.040 --> 01:15:39.476
And I'll get you to the finish line,
because I know I can.


01:15:39.600 --> 01:15:42.319
But you have to let me finish
what I've started.


01:15:42.440 --> 01:15:43.839
You have to.


01:15:46.160 --> 01:15:48.151
You're the only hope for a cure.


01:15:50.240 --> 01:15:52.151
- OK.
- Ange,


01:15:52.280 --> 01:15:55.272
you cannot let them
turn you into a lab rat.


01:15:56.880 --> 01:15:57.949
(Angela) Oh, shit!


01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:01.274
Go!


01:16:01.400 --> 01:16:02.799
Move!


01:16:15.800 --> 01:16:17.199
Abraxon, through the gates.


01:16:24.560 --> 01:16:25.788
(Cole) Hold on!


01:16:46.600 --> 01:16:48.158
(Groaning)


01:17:10.240 --> 01:17:12.037
Ange?


01:17:22.400 --> 01:17:25.039
(Choking)


01:18:20.120 --> 01:18:21.792
It's all right.


01:18:35.320 --> 01:18:38.392
(Growling)


01:18:42.400 --> 01:18:44.152
- Katie!
- No, no, no, no!


01:18:45.280 --> 01:18:46.269
I'm sorry.


01:18:46.400 --> 01:18:48.755
Stay quiet. Stay quiet.


01:18:48.880 --> 01:18:51.553
(Snarling)


01:19:31.680 --> 01:19:33.079
Let's go.


01:19:35.120 --> 01:19:36.519
No.


01:19:37.320 --> 01:19:38.719
Let us go, Cole.


01:19:38.840 --> 01:19:41.673
Let us go. You know
what they're going to do to her,


01:19:42.440 --> 01:19:45.159
I can't let that happen.
You four, you take the helicopter.


01:19:45.280 --> 01:19:48.477
We'll take that truck there.
It's like a tank. Everybody wins.


01:19:48.600 --> 01:19:51.239
- No, you won't stand a chance, Joe.
- Well, we can try.


01:19:55.880 --> 01:19:58.110
I have to do this.


01:19:58.240 --> 01:19:59.878
For everyone's sake.


01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:00.989
- Come on.
- Angie!


01:20:01.120 --> 01:20:02.599
I can't let you do this!


01:20:18.160 --> 01:20:19.639
Matt?


01:20:22.680 --> 01:20:24.671
We're not going anywhere!


01:20:30.800 --> 01:20:31.994
Fuck!


01:20:33.120 --> 01:20:34.712
Now what do we do?


01:20:35.760 --> 01:20:37.637
- Angie.
- Matt, oh.


01:20:38.640 --> 01:20:39.959
Are you OK?


01:20:40.080 --> 01:20:42.833
Listen, I've got a Zodiac on the river.


01:20:42.960 --> 01:20:45.838
The HMS Valiant
is ten miles downstream to the east.


01:20:45.960 --> 01:20:48.394
Whatever these things are,
they fucking hate water.


01:20:48.520 --> 01:20:50.238
So I think we can make it, OK?


01:20:50.360 --> 01:20:52.510
- I don't even know you.
- Trust him.


01:20:52.640 --> 01:20:54.039
- Are you sure?
- I'm sure.


01:20:54.160 --> 01:20:56.071
Just trust him. He's my brother.


01:20:56.520 --> 01:20:57.919
- Come on, Joe.
- OK, let's go.


01:20:58.040 --> 01:20:59.758
Come on! Let's go!


01:21:03.080 --> 01:21:04.718
Oh, Geoffrey!


01:21:04.840 --> 01:21:06.671
Geoffrey! Help him!


01:21:06.800 --> 01:21:09.155
Geoffrey!


01:21:09.280 --> 01:21:10.679
- Go and get the boat ready now.
- What's happening?


01:21:10.800 --> 01:21:12.950
Leave him. He's got it.
Nothing you can do. Go.


01:21:13.080 --> 01:21:17.153
- Come on.
- You fucking help him!


01:21:17.280 --> 01:21:19.236
Or I'll kill her.


01:21:19.360 --> 01:21:21.430
- No.
- I'll scream.


01:21:22.240 --> 01:21:25.391
- I'll scream so loud they'll all come.
- No, you won't.


01:21:25.520 --> 01:21:27.112
Help him. Help him!


01:21:30.040 --> 01:21:31.837
You let her go now.


01:21:39.400 --> 01:21:40.753
Get to the boat. Go.


01:21:40.880 --> 01:21:43.269
Give me the gun.


01:21:45.400 --> 01:21:48.756
Lavie, don't leave me.


01:21:55.240 --> 01:21:57.629
- I'm coming with you.
- No, you're not.


01:21:57.760 --> 01:22:00.957
You should never
have threatened her, ever.


01:22:20.960 --> 01:22:22.393
I just wanted to save you.


01:22:22.520 --> 01:22:25.159
They're coming, they're coming!


01:22:46.720 --> 01:22:48.119
What the hell's he doing here?


01:22:48.240 --> 01:22:49.832
(Growling)


01:22:49.960 --> 01:22:51.871
Angie, watch out!


01:22:52.000 --> 01:22:54.389
(Roaring)


01:22:56.760 --> 01:22:58.557
Matt! Matt!


01:22:59.480 --> 01:23:00.879
Matt!


01:23:09.120 --> 01:23:11.554
No. No! No, don't!


01:23:11.680 --> 01:23:13.318
Just get her on the boat!


01:23:16.680 --> 01:23:17.874
No!


01:23:18.000 --> 01:23:19.194
No!


01:23:30.440 --> 01:23:32.192
Just take her and go.


01:23:32.320 --> 01:23:33.833
Oi, no, Joe, come on.


01:23:33.960 --> 01:23:35.439
You're coming with us.


01:23:40.440 --> 01:23:41.429
I can't.


01:23:44.160 --> 01:23:45.559
Oh, Joe!


01:23:45.680 --> 01:23:47.511
It's OK.


01:23:47.640 --> 01:23:50.108
It's all right, it's all right.


01:23:50.240 --> 01:23:52.117
I can't be without you again.


01:23:57.040 --> 01:23:58.393
You won't be.


01:24:10.080 --> 01:24:12.116
Angela!


01:24:12.240 --> 01:24:14.356
You do the right thing.


01:24:19.600 --> 01:24:20.999
I love you.


01:24:27.880 --> 01:24:29.029
Just go.


01:24:29.160 --> 01:24:30.479
Go.


01:24:55.240 --> 01:24:58.312
(Cole) 'I've done so many bad things
in my life.'


01:25:00.360 --> 01:25:02.954
But I'm not asking for forgiveness.


01:25:13.720 --> 01:25:16.598
'Because I've had my shot
at redemption.


01:25:16.720 --> 01:25:18.950
'And every second chance,


01:25:19.080 --> 01:25:21.071
'well, it comes with a price.'


01:25:50.560 --> 01:25:52.551
- You ready?
- I'm ready.


01:25:53.920 --> 01:25:55.751
You've done good, Joe.


01:25:58.560 --> 01:26:00.437
'Two of us needed her first.


01:26:02.000 --> 01:26:04.116
'And now she can save the rest.'


01:27:02.480 --> 01:27:04.277
I'm sorry, Ange.


01:27:04.400 --> 01:27:05.753
I'm so sorry.


01:27:08.880 --> 01:27:10.598
Come on, let's go. Let's go.


01:27:15.560 --> 01:27:17.152
What did that guy mean?


01:27:18.320 --> 01:27:21.392
When he said, "Do the right thing",
what did he mean?


01:27:21.520 --> 01:27:23.511
I need to see some doctors.


01:27:23.640 --> 01:27:25.039
As soon as I can.


01:27:33.920 --> 01:27:36.195
(Radio) 'This is HMS Valiant to Control.


01:27:36.320 --> 01:27:38.880
'We are now proceeding
en route to safe zone.


01:27:39.000 --> 01:27:41.309
'Confirm we have picked up two civilians.


01:27:41.440 --> 01:27:43.874
'Request immediate transfer
of female adult


01:27:44.000 --> 01:27:46.468
'to infection control research unit.


01:27:46.600 --> 01:27:48.033
'Over and out.'


01:27:48.160 --> 01:27:50.390
(Cole) So, my time has come.


01:27:51.640 --> 01:27:53.870
Being part of this world I helped create.


01:27:59.840 --> 01:28:01.478
I'll die with it.


01:28:13.880 --> 01:28:16.553
(Powers up chainsaw)


01:28:17.200 --> 01:28:19.111
(# Heavy metal)

